
# Shell/python deployed to Linux must stay LF — a CRLF heredoc terminator
# makes bash report "unexpected end of file" only once it is on the server.
#
# ALL of them, not just scripts/. The pin was scripts/-only while the scripts
# that actually run on the box live elsewhere too — vaultchat-backend/deploy.sh
# and smoke-test.sh had no eol attribute at all, and the root apply*.sh none
# either. They survive today only because this checkout happens to have
# core.autocrlf=true, which is per-machine config, not a property of the repo —
# exactly the thing an attribute is for.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
